  "raw_text": "No. A 10% month-over-month decline alone doesn’t establish that the campaign failed.\n\nYou would need to compare sales against a credible baseline, such as:\n\n- Expected sales without the campaign\n- The same month last year, adjusted for seasonality\n- A control group or untreated market\n- Campaign goals beyond immediate sales, such as leads, awareness, or retention\n- Other factors: pricing, inventory, competitors, holidays, economic conditions, or channel changes\n\nSales may have fallen 10% but could have fallen more without the campaign. Evaluate incremental impact and ROI against the campaign’s predefined objectives before concluding it failed.",
